    Each level after first adds one Healing or Physical power; levels 2, 4, 5,
    6, 8, 10, 12 and 15 add one Super power as well - two schedule slots at
    those levels. Mind Bleeder powers are excluded by the book; they are their
    own catalog category, so the Super gate already excludes them.
  - I.S.P. regained at 4 per hour of activity or 20 per hour of meditation or
    sleep (printed 68) - not a schema field; in GM Notes.
  - Saves (printed 68): +3 "vs mind control drugs and magic" stored as
    saves.mind_control 3. Horror Factor +1 at levels 1, 3, 4, 6, 9, 12, 15.
    Master psychic saves vs psionics at 10 or higher - in GM Notes.
  - Impervious to vampire bite/mind control, Mind Bleeder powers and
    possession are immunities, not bonuses - special_abilities.
  - P.P.E. is P.E. attribute number + 4D6 (printed 68).
  - Skills (printed 68): "Languages: Two of choice" - no separate native
    tongue line is printed, so none is granted. Lore one of choice enumerates
    the setting lores (judgement). "Mathematics only" under Science taken as
    both Basic and Advanced (judgement). Rogue "except Computer Hacking and
    Ventriloquism": the catalog files Ventriloquism under Technical, so the
    exclusion is placed on Technical. Military is CS-trained only, so it is left out of the categories and kept in the note (book-reconcile); the
    Communications +5% (human) and Wilderness +5% (Psi-Stalker) are
    conditional and not stored as bonuses. Espionage "Tracking" is the
    catalog''s "Tracking (people)".
  - Hand to Hand: Expert may become Martial Arts, or Assassin if evil, for
    one related skill (printed 68).
  - Equipment: the book prints two packages (printed 68-69). The Independent
    package is stored; the CS Operative package (Dead Boy armor, CS energy
    rifle and sidearm with 4 E-clips each, survival knife, two vibro-blades,
    neural mace, four grenades, a non-energy weapon, large flashlight, 1D4
    handcuffs, three flares, air filter and gas mask, distancing binoculars,
    tinted goggles, utility belt, walkie-talkie, dress uniform, combat boots,
    canteen, plus issue-on-assignment gear) is in GM Notes. "Black jumpsuit"
    is stored as clothing; "1D4 medium-sized sacks" as sack; "3-6 wooden
    stakes" as 1D4+2; "silver cross" as small-silver-cross; "Neuro-Mace or
    Electro-Stunner (Rifts Lone Star)" - no Electro-Stunner row exists, so the
    neural-mace is granted. Hover cycle starts battered (-2D6% M.D.C.) - not
    stored.
  - Money (printed 69): independents 2D6x1000 credits plus Black Market items
    worth 2D4x100 credits (the goods are not stored). CS troops: Psi-Stalker
    Nullifiers get 30% more than ordinary Psi-Stalkers, humans the same as ISS
    operatives - no figure printed here.
  - Race restrictions: humans (70%) and Psi-Stalkers (30%). Attribute
    requirements: none (high I.Q., M.E. and P.S. helpful). Alignment any,
    leaning selfish and good. Cybernetics: starts with none, medical use only.
---

## Lore

The Psi-Nullifier is a human master psionic or a Psi-Stalker whose reactive mental defenses have grown into a field of negative psychic energy that smothers psionics and magic around him. It is rare - about one Psi-Stalker in two hundred and one master psionic in a thousand - and usually follows a childhood brush with powerful magic, psionics or the supernatural. The defense is mostly involuntary, firing on its own whenever mental or mystic force is turned on him or unleashed close by. The Coalition States prize these psychics and run a harsh training program that turns most of its young reactive psychics into Nullifiers, several hundred of whom serve in Psi-Battalion, the ISS and other CS forces as anti-psychic and anti-supernatural specialists, trackers and spies. Independent Nullifiers find steady, dangerous work hunting monsters, evil psychics and rogue magic users.

## GM Notes

**Saving throws:** as a Master Psychic the Psi-Nullifier needs 10 or higher to save vs psionic attack.

**I.S.P.:** 3D6x10 plus M.E., +2D4+2 per level. Regained at 4 per hour of activity, or 20 per hour of meditation or sleep.

**Nullification bookkeeping:** the automatic 1D6 negative I.S.P. is spent every time a power or spell targets him or goes off within 10 feet, including several in one melee, so a Nullifier under sustained psychic attack drains his own reserve quickly. A caster or psychic who knows what they face can overspend to punch through, and the Nullifier can answer by deliberately spending more.

**CS Operative equipment (instead of the Independent package):** Dead Boy body armor, CS energy rifle and energy sidearm of choice with 4 extra E-clips for each, survival knife, two vibro-blades, neural mace, four grenades, one non-energy weapon of choice, large flashlight, 1D4 pairs of handcuffs, three signal flares, air filter and gas mask, distancing binoculars, tinted goggles, utility belt, walkie-talkie, dress uniform, combat boots and canteen. Other weapons, vehicles, ammunition and rations are issued per mission at the commanding officer''s discretion, with heavy weapons and vehicles rarely assigned. CS pay replaces starting money: Psi-Stalker Nullifiers earn 30% more than ordinary Psi-Stalkers, humans the same as ISS operatives.

**Independent extras:** Black Market items worth 2D4x100 credits beside the 2D6x1000 credits; the hover cycle option starts battered (reduce M.D.C. by 2D6%).
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-nullifier');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-nullifier';

